1
00:04:41,538 --> 00:04:47,538
Kinky Boots: The Musical is a music, comedy film directed by Brett Sullivan.

2
00:09:23,076 --> 00:09:29,076
Charlie is a factory owner struggling to save his family business, and
Lola is a fabulous entertainer with a wildly exciting idea.

3
00:14:04,615 --> 00:14:10,615
With a little compassion and a lot of understanding, this unexpected pair learn to embrace their
differences and create a line of sturdy stilettos unlike any the world has ever seen!

4
00:18:46,153 --> 00:18:52,153
Charlie Price, played by Killian Donnelly.

5
00:23:27,692 --> 00:23:33,692
Lola/Simon, played by Matt Henry.

6
00:28:09,230 --> 00:28:15,230
Lauren, played by Natalie McQueen.

7
00:32:50,769 --> 00:32:56,769
Don, played by Sean Needham.

8
00:37:32,307 --> 00:37:38,307
Nicola, played by Cordelia Farnworth.

9
00:42:13,846 --> 00:42:19,846
George, played by Antony Reed.

10
00:46:55,384 --> 00:47:01,384
Kinky Boots is a musical with music and lyrics by Cyndi
Lauper and book by Harvey Fierstein.

11
00:51:36,923 --> 00:51:42,923
Based on the 2005 British film Kinky Boots, written by Geoff Deane and Tim Firth and
mostly inspired by true events, the musical tells the story of Charlie Price.

12
00:56:18,461 --> 00:56:24,461
Having inherited a shoe factory from his father, Charlie forms an unlikely partnership with cabaret
performer and drag queen Lola to produce a line of high-heeled boots and save the business.

13
01:01:00,000 --> 01:01:06,000
In the process, Charlie and Lola discover that
they are not so different after all.

14
01:05:41,538 --> 01:05:47,538
Following the show's conception in 2006, the
creative team was assembled by 2010.

15
01:10:23,076 --> 01:10:29,076
The original production of Kinky Boots premiered at the Bank of America Theatre in Chicago in October 2012, with both direction
and choreography by Jerry Mitchell, and starring Stark Sands and Billy Porter as Charlie and Lola, respectively.

16
01:15:04,615 --> 01:15:10,615
It made its Broadway debut at the Al Hirschfeld Theatre on April 4,
2013, following previews that began on March 3, 2013.

17
01:19:46,153 --> 01:19:52,153
The musical began a US tour in 2014.

18
01:24:27,692 --> 01:24:33,692
The Broadway production ended its six-year run on April 7, 2019.

19
01:29:09,230 --> 01:29:15,230
Having initially been less well received by theatre critics and at the box office than another 2013 Broadway
production, Matilda the Musical, Kinky Boots entered the 2013 awards season as an underdog.

20
01:33:50,769 --> 01:33:56,769
However, less than a month after opening, Kinky Boots surpassed this rival with audiences in
weekly box office gross and later enjoyed a post-Tony boost in advance sales.

21
01:38:32,307 --> 01:38:38,307
The production earned a season-high 13 nominations and 6 Tony wins, including Best Musical, Best Actor for Billy Porter and Best
Score for Lauper in her first outing as a Broadway songwriter, making her the first woman to win alone in that category.

22
01:43:13,846 --> 01:43:19,846
The musical's cast album premiered at number one on the Billboard Cast
Albums Chart and number fifty-one on the Billboard 200 chart.

23
01:47:55,384 --> 01:48:01,384
Making its West End debut in 2015, in 2016, it won three
Laurence Olivier Awards, including Best New Musical.

24
01:52:36,923 --> 01:52:42,923
The film explores themes of drag queen, musical,
stage show, filmed theater, gay theme.

25
01:57:18,461 --> 01:57:24,461
The tone is lighthearted.
